1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,078
What happens if you sleep in your contact lenses?

2
00:00:03,338 --> 00:00:05,460
Your cornea has no blood vessels.

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:07,898
It gets its oxygen straight from the air.

4
00:00:08,158 --> 00:00:11,299
A lens plus a closed eyelid cuts that supply off.

5
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:13,450
The surface starves, then weakens.

6
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:16,272
Micro-tears open in the starved cornea.

7
00:00:16,532 --> 00:00:18,720
Bacteria like Pseudomonas move in.

8
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:21,318
Their enzymes digest the cornea, fast.

9
00:00:21,578 --> 00:00:23,624
By morning, a red, painful ulcer.

10
00:00:23,884 --> 00:00:27,114
In rare cases, a scar or a corneal transplant.

11
00:00:27,374 --> 00:00:30,505
So take your lenses out before bed, every time.

12
00:00:30,765 --> 00:00:32,606
And never let them touch tap water.
